# Default-ignore policy (2026-06-07 user rule): ignore build scaffolding, secrets,
# and temporary/working files by default. Only files we INTEND to commit are tracked
# — un-ignore them deliberately. Keep this file current as the build creates new
# temp artifacts. The user is always the one who commits; the assistant never does.

# Build scaffolding — meta-tooling used to BUILD the package, not the shipped package
/.claude/
/.claude-backups/
CLAUDE.md

# Dependencies & build output
node_modules/
dist/

# Secrets & environment
.env
*.secret

# Temporary / working files (debug screenshots, scratch, logs, caches)
*.log
*.tmp
tmp/
scratch/
screenshots/
.cache/

# @playwright/mcp run output (navigation snapshot YAMLs, generated at runtime)
.playwright-mcp/
